# No Windows line endings

All text in this repo must use **Unix LF** (`\n`). Do not write **CRLF** (`\r\n`) or mix the two in one file.

## Prohibited

- Saving or committing `\r\n` in any text file
- Introducing CRLF via Write / StrReplace / generated output
- Leaving CRLF in place because a file is third-party, historical, or a fixture

```text
# ❌ BAD — CRLF
const x = 1;\r\n

# ✅ GOOD — LF
const x = 1;\n
```

## Required instead

- Write every new or edited text file with LF only
- If a text file has `\r`, convert it to LF
- Git attribute `* text=auto eol=lf` keeps checkouts LF; do not override it

## Out of scope (do not rewrite)

- Binary files
- `submodules/**`

## Check

```bash
git ls-files --eol | awk '$0 !~ /submodules\// && ($2 ~ /w\/crlf/ || $2 ~ /w\/mixed/)'
```
